              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to have a good time, then the Persian for to become a member."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اسکی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اسکی (eski) — \"skiing; a ski\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زمستانها برای اسکی به کوه میرویم. zemestânhâ barâ-ye eski be kuh miravim. In winter we go to the mountains to ski."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "eski kardan — to ski. Persian puts e- before the sk- cluster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "eski was borrowed from French ski, which EtymDB traces to Norwegian ski and Old Norse skíð, 'stick of wood, snowshoe' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
